/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 48 0 R
/T (3. Theory: JavaScript provides different types of functions, such as function declarations, function expressions, and arrow functions, to perform reusable tasks efficiently. Variable scope controls where variables can be accessed and includes global, function, and block scope. A closure is a feature in which an inner function remembers and accesses variables from its outer function even after the outer function has finished execution. JavaScript also supports exception handling through the try-catch statement, which helps detect and manage runtime errors without stopping the program. In this practical, these concepts are applied to develop a palindrome checker, which verifies whether a given string or number reads the same forwards and backwards, demonstrating the practical use of functions, scope, closures, and error handling. )
/E (3. Theory: JavaScript provides different types of functions, such as function declarations, function expressions, and arrow functions, to perform reusable tasks efficiently. Variable scope controls where variables can be accessed and includes global, function, and block scope. A closure is a feature in which an inner function remembers and accesses variables from its outer function even after the outer function has finished execution. JavaScript also supports exception handling through the try-catch statement, which helps detect and manage runtime errors without stopping the program. In this practical, these concepts are applied to develop a palindrome checker, which verifies whether a given string or number reads the same forwards and backwards, demonstrating the practical use of functions, scope, closures, and error handling. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
